<task id="SRFR-041" project="set-regarding-and-field-mapping-resolver-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>sprk_todo FormXml revert — hide OOB fields again (undo SRFR-038 visibility flip; preserve OnLoad handler wiring)</title>
    <status>completed</status>
    <estimated-effort>30min</estimated-effort>
    <actual-effort>~15min</actual-effort>
    <assigned>AI Agent</assigned>
    <started>2026-07-03</started>
    <completed>2026-07-03</completed>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-group>—</parallel-group>
    <tags>form-config,formxml,sprk-todo,dataverse-deploy,wave-3-followon,post-v1.3.3,revert</tags>
    <depends-on>SRFR-038</depends-on>
    <wave>3</wave>
  </metadata>

  <prompt><![CDATA[
Post-SRFR-038 owner clarification. SRFR-038 misinterpreted the owner's
intent: the OOB fields on the form (sprk_regardingrecordnumber +
sprk_regardingrecordname cells) were ALREADY hidden by owner intentionally,
NOT hidden by a SRFR-036 regression. SRFR-038 made them visible — WRONG.

Revert: flip both cells back to `visible="false"` while preserving
everything else that SRFR-036 + SRFR-038 established:
  - Cell IDs unchanged
  - `disabled="true"` preserved
  - `<events>` block + `<formLibraries>` block preserved (companion
    webresource stays wired — owner may re-enable fields via maker portal
    later)
  - URL cell (sprk_regardingrecordurl) preserved in its current hidden state
  - Section `celllabelposition="Top"` preserved
  - All other sections untouched

Deliverables:
  1. Author revert deploy script mirroring SRFR-038's PS1 pattern (Get-Token,
     Invoke-Dv helpers, PATCH systemform + PublishXml).
  2. Deploy: PATCH systemforms(eca59df4-1364-f111-ab0c-7ced8ddc4cc6) with the
     reverted formxml, then PublishXml for sprk_todo entity.
  3. Verify: re-fetch formxml, confirm both cells now `visible="false"`,
     section intact, OnLoad handler still registered.

Constraints:
  - ADR-006: form config only, no PCF code changes.
  - Preserve SRFR-036 companion webresource registration (`<events>` +
    `<formLibraries>` block wiring).
  - Preserve `sprk_regardingrecordurl` cell's hidden state.
  - Preserve `disabled="true"` on both new-shape fields.
  - Idempotent: script detects if fix has already been applied.

Step 9.5 quality gates: SKIPPED per STANDARD rigor (form config, not code).

Coordination: SRFR-039 running in parallel bumping RegardingResolver PCF to
v1.3.4 (restore Name cell inline). Different files, no collision.
  ]]></prompt>

  <role>Dataverse FormXml surgery + systemform PATCH developer familiar
  with MDA main-form section/row/cell layout, cell-level visibility, and
  direct Web API systemform PATCH + PublishXml deploy pattern (mirrors
  SRFR-036 + SRFR-038 deploy scripts).</role>

  <goal><![CDATA[
Owner-visible outcome: on the sprk_todo main form (after hard-refresh),
the OOB sprk_regardingrecordnumber + sprk_regardingrecordname cells are
BOTH hidden (per owner intent — they exist on the form for other purposes
but not displayed). RegardingResolver PCF (v1.3.4 from SRFR-039)
displays the record-number + record-name inline in its Row 2. Companion
webresource OnLoad handler remains registered so owner can re-enable the
OOB fields via maker portal later if desired.
  ]]></goal>

  <inputs>
    <file purpose="prior-log">projects/set-regarding-and-field-mapping-resolver-r1/notes/task-038-sprk-todo-form-labels.log</file>
    <file purpose="prior-task">projects/set-regarding-and-field-mapping-resolver-r1/tasks/038-sprk-todo-form-labels-fix.poml</file>
    <file purpose="prior-task">projects/set-regarding-and-field-mapping-resolver-r1/tasks/036-sprk-todo-form-config.poml</file>
